    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nAll\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be helpful to have a \"loaded\" variable, similar to other vim plugins such as https://github.com/glepnir/galaxyline.nvim/blob/main/plugin/galaxyline.vim. This recommendation is also further outlined in https://vimways.org/2019/writing-vim-plugin/ and https://vi.stackexchange.com/questions/26132/why-do-plugins-have-to-check-if-they-are-already-loaded.\r\n\r\nI make use of these variables to optionally enable certain settings depending on if a plugin is available or not. ",
    "closed_at": "2022-09-13T14:32:46Z",
