    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The recommended way to check if module 'mini.xxx' is \"active\" is with `_G.MiniXxx ~= nil` Lua snippet. For example, the 'mini.surround' check is `_G.MiniSurround ~= nil`.\r\n\r\nSome clarification. Every module of this plugin is an independent Lua module which should be set up explicitly via `require('mini.xxx').setup()` (except some cases which only provide Lua functions). Every `setup()` call creates a global variable `_G.MiniXxx` (that is [by design](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim#general-principles) and always be like that). This is also the way 'mini.nvim' itself uses in rare occasions when it needs such a check (like in [mini.starter](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/02e22656f1b78aa9f9a678e0ff31b62bbaf0dee6/lua/mini/starter.lua#L456-L458)).\r\n\r\nDoes this solve your problem?",
            "created_at": "2022-09-13T06:42:14Z",
