        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "That is close to what I want, but since that variable is only set when the plugin is required, it didn't quite fix it. \r\n\r\nEssentially I wanted to add a check that only called \"require('mini.surround').setup()\" if it could detect that mini.nvim was installed. The global variable \"g:loaded_*\" allows you to check for that. I think it is an old vimscript-ism, and isn't necessary anymore with lua. \r\n\r\nI ended up writing a checker for lua modules instead using something similar to https://stackoverflow.com/questions/15429236/how-to-check-if-a-module-exists-in-lua, which fixes my issue.\r\n\r\nThanks for your quick reply!",
            "created_at": "2022-09-13T14:32:46Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/129#issuecomment-1245503606",
            "id": 1245503606,
